    "description": "Integration boundary between IntelliDealer Core (ID) and eServiceTech.\n\nID is the system of record for work-order, customer, equipment, billing and\nfinancial transactions; eServiceTech supports field-service execution.\n\n## Authentication\n\nMachine-to-machine only, via OAuth2 **client credentials**. Exchange your\nclient ID and secret at `/api/v1/oauth/token` for a bearer token,\nthen send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens are least-privilege:\na route rejects any token missing a scope it declares.\n\n## Tenancy\n\nThe deployment is multi-tenant and dealer-scoped. Every access token carries\nan authoritative `dealer_id`, and all reads, writes, replay and reconciliation\nare filtered by it. `X-Dealer-Id` may be sent to assert intent, but it must\nmatch the token — a mismatch is refused, never coerced.\n\n## Correlation\n\nEvery request is assigned a correlation ID, returned in `X-Correlation-Id`.\nSend your own to stitch this call into an existing trace. The ID appears on\nsuccess and error responses alike so any exchange stays traceable end-to-end.\n\n## Error model\n\nFailures share one envelope carrying a stable `code`, a `category` from the\ntaxonomy below, and an explicit `retryable` flag — so a caller never has to\ninfer retry safety from the HTTP status.\n\n| Category | Meaning | Retryable |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `TRANSPORT_ERROR` | Timeout, DNS, connection, TLS, or gateway failure. | yes |\n| `AUTH_ERROR` | Expired token, invalid credential, or insufficient scope. | no |\n| `SCHEMA_ERROR` | Missing or invalid field, or unsupported format. | no |\n| `REFERENCE_DATA_ERROR` | Unknown customer, equipment, technician, part, or job. | no |\n| `BUSINESS_RULE_ERROR` | Invalid state transition, invalid quantity, or duplicate posting. | no |\n| `CONCURRENCY_ERROR` | Object changed since the source read it. | yes |\n| `ATTACHMENT_ERROR` | Unsupported file type, size exceeded, or inaccessible reference. | no |\n| `SYSTEM_ERROR` | Target service unavailable or internal failure. | yes |\n\n## Rate limits\n\nGeneral traffic is capped at 600 requests per\n60s. Credential exchange is capped separately at\n20 **failed** attempts per window — successful exchanges are not\ncounted, so a correctly configured client can always refresh. Responses carry\n`RateLimit` headers, and a 429 carries `Retry-After`.\n\n## Versioning\n\nThe major version is carried in the path (`/api/v1`). Additive changes\nship in place; breaking changes ship under a new major version."
  },
